<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Jan 4.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - Jan 4.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended January 4:</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE    % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				 (RS MLN)</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   182	   0.58     327050  59.52    16.62</p>
<p>Tata Power	   129	   0.44     160950  20.76    17.79</p>
<p>Tata Engg	    360	   1.23     118250  42.57    17.82</p>
<p>State Bank	   245	   0.77     330100  80.87    16.39</p>
<p>Reliance	     215	   0.68     221900  47.71    16.49</p>
<p>MTNL		   235	   0.70	93000  21.86    15.53</p>
<p>L&amp;T		    230	   0.64	80850  18.60    14.51</p>
<p>Hind Lever	   810	   2.39	12850  10.41    15.39</p>
<p>Colgate		240	   0.87	41250   9.90    18.90</p>
<p>BSES		   220	   0.41	97550  21.46     9.72</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 16.15 percent on an annualised basis against 15.71 percent in the previous carry forward account ended December 21.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
